## What to generate

This project's cockpit scripts ship as **runnable placeholders** with annotated
`# ── CONFIGURE ──` blocks. Your job is to explore `@@APP_NAME@@` and fill them in:

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `tmux-cockpit.sh` | remote/k8s cockpit — log windows, port-forward, worker priming |
| `tmux-cockpit-local.sh` | local dev cockpit — backend window + workers |

For a fresh scaffold, fill in `# ── CONFIGURE ──` defaults and project overlay
sections. Existing launchers/overlays are project-owned: do not overwrite or
regenerate them on upgrade. Present explicit changes for owner review.

Follow global `setup-e2e-cockpit` for distinct absolute control/queue roots
(`docs/cockpit-control`, `docs/cockpit-queue`), shell exports and tmux injection.
Bootstrap with `cockpit-control init` or `bind-roots` using explicit queue,
planning and repeatable implementation roots; pass `preflight` before work.
Install complete tools/modules via toolkit `bootstrap.sh global` /
`codex-global`, never a standalone executable copied from the harness.

Preserve the global durable contract in both `.agents` and `.github` overlays:
FIFO/tick only; `dispatch --bootstrap` only primes roles. `accept-dispatch`
starts only on `accepted` / `start_work=true` (sequence 1; pending dispatch is
0 without heartbeat); `heartbeat` running starts at 2. `ask` / `access-prompt`
use private typed body refs; `pending` / `read-question` return mission-status
JSON. Only explicit human replies; `hold --answers` never approves. Inspect
`status.pending_commands` / `command-status`; accepted-worker cancel/replace
requires accepted then applied ACK with matching digest and typed `--result`.
Reuse IDs/digests, journal no secrets, keep lifecycle separate from pane
diagnosis, and never use raw `send`/`nudge` for mission/approval/cancel.
Follow the global scheduler example: all five intent fields and stored
root/session/window, read-only `--dry-run`, `stop` alias of `cancel` including
fired recurring jobs. Legacy `migrate` diagnoses only: explicitly stop old jobs,
bootstrap/bind/preflight, then reschedule. No corrupt-state renaming or job rewrite.

